  "line": 20,
  "title": "Cached gate results and stored handles are reused without checking the commit they ran on",
  "detail": "`runGateExecution` returns `gateResults.values[purpose]`, or attaches the stored `gateExecution.handle`, whenever the stage, round and purpose match. It never compares `gateResults.sha` or `handle.request.headSha` with the checkout's current head. The ordinary gates stage has a `checkedSha` guard on gate evidence, but the rebase gates in `mergeForDelivery` (engine.ts ~2389) have none, and `completeMerge` runs only when head equals `before` (engine.ts:2381), so a resumed delivery accepts whatever merge commit is checked out. Reproduced with a temporary test: an injected executor checked merge M1, the checkout then held M2 with the same parents, and the daemon was killed at the `gate-started` checkpoint, and again at the `gate-result` checkpoint. On resume the run succeeded and published M2 with zero new executions in both cases. With a sha comparison added, both cases refused. Fix: before reusing either a cached result or a stored handle, compare the recorded sha with `headSha(cwd)`. On a mismatch, discard both and run fresh. Slice 2's remote executors depend on the same pin. Test: restart at both checkpoints with the head moved, and assert a new execution happens (or the stage refuses) and the moved commit is never published on the old result."
 },
 {
  "id": "F2",
  "file": "src/pipeline/engine.ts",
  "line": 1157,
  "title": "A restart during a pending retry replays it without the setup it depends on",
  "detail": "Retries run with `setup: []` because on main they follow the first attempt in the same checkout, after its setup. After a restart, the gates stage calls `checkoutCommitted` (removing ignored dependencies and build output), `runGateExecution` returns the cached `initial` result (gate-execution.ts:23), and the stored regression-retry handle then replays only the selected checks, with no setup. Reproduced with a real local setup command that creates `node_modules/ready`, and a check that needs it and fails transiently once. Uninterrupted, the retry passes (flaky). Killed at the retry's `gate-started` checkpoint and resumed, the retry fails with `missing-setup`, the check is recorded as regressed and blocking, and the run spends another implementation round. Main re-runs the whole stage, setup included, on resume. Baseline retries have the same exposure after prepare's cleanup. Fix, whichever is smaller: either (a) drop the completed-result cache for local and replay the stage from the start on resume, as main does, discarding a stored handle for a later purpose; or (b) make a replayed retry run the stage's setup before its checks. The second is also what a fresh remote checkout will need. Test: the setup-dependent check above, killed during the retry and resumed, gives the same verdict as uninterrupted."
 },
 {
  "id": "F3",
  "file": "src/gates/executor.ts",
  "line": 124,
  "title": "Gate hooks reach only the local executor; an injected executor's events are dropped",
  "detail": "`executeGate` passes `hooks` only into `localExecutor(hooks)`. When `injected` is used (the seam's purpose), `onResult` is never called: that feeds the engine's per-check gate events and the land queue's log (`appendFileSync` in land/queue.ts:397). `onWait` and `holder` are dropped too. `execution.events` is produced by the local executor, but nothing in `executeGate` or its callers iterates it. Production only uses local today, so nothing visible breaks yet, but a second executor would silently lose gate events and land logs. Fix: make `executeGate` the one place that turns execution events into hook calls (setup and check results, so the land log keeps its setup lines), and have the local executor report through its events rather than calling `hooks.onResult` directly, so a result is reported once. Test: inject a fake executor that emits a setup and a check result, and assert the land log contains both lines and the run gets the gate event."
 },
 {
