  "title": "Redacted display data is executed and matched as if it were the real request",
  "detail": "The persisted handle is `redactGateData(handle)`, including `request.gates`, and after a restart the local executor runs the stored request. Results are also redacted (line 50) before the retry functions compare `result.command` with `cfg.checks[].run` literally (run.ts:181, :276), and before `cacheableBaseline` compares commands. Reproduced with a gate command containing a registered synthetic credential: the failed baseline got no retry because `echo [redacted]` no longer matched, and replaying the persisted handle executed the redacted text and failed where the original passed. Fix: keep display data and executable data apart. Persist an identity (stage, round, purpose, id) and rebuild the request from the trusted gate config the caller already holds (`ctx.state.gatesConfig` / the `req` passed to `executeGate`). Compare unredacted results, and redact where results are stored or shown."
 },
 {
